# Supplemental failure diagnostics

These 14 raw serialized payloads are seven pairs: `.java.bin` is the normative Java V1 encoding, `.go.bin` the pinned Go encoding. Four pairs match; three deliberately differ and remain OPEN compatibility issues. They are outside the unchanged original29 sample set.

`manifest.json` records source commits, input semantics, protocol/serializer/compressor, per-file length/hash and classification. [Source and reproducible exporter](../../../../../tools/go-failure-variants/README.md), [runtime evidence](../../../../../docs/phase-0/evidence/local-failure-variants-20261112/README.md), [known differences](../../../../../docs/phase-0/known-go-v1-failure-divergences.md).

Never count a correctly detected mismatch as a successful cross-language roundtrip. The fixed Go source remains unpatched.
